1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,433
Tree planting now dominates political and popular agendas and is often presented as an

2
00:00:06,433 --> 00:00:11,744
easy answer to the climate crisis, as well as a way for business corporations

3
00:00:11,744 --> 00:00:14,610
to offset their carbon emissions.

4
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:20,570
But unfortunately, tree planting isn’t as straightforward as some people think.

5
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:25,268
When the wrong trees are planted in the wrong place, it can do considerably

6
00:00:25,268 --> 00:00:30,750
more damage than good, failing to help either people or the environment.

7
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:37,027
Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken on a huge scale in many countries

8
00:00:37,027 --> 00:00:41,520
and it’s crucial that the right trees are selected.

9
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:48,359
A mix of species should always be planted, typical of the local natural forest ecosystem

10
00:00:48,359 --> 00:00:55,660
and including rare and endangered species in order to create a rich ecosystem.

11
00:00:55,660 --> 00:01:00,590
It’s important to avoid non-native species that could become invasive.

12
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:07,329
Invasive species are a significant contributor to the current global biodiversity crisis

13
00:01:07,329 --> 00:01:15,130
and are often in competition with native species and may threaten their long-term survival.

14
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:22,526
Restoring biodiversity that will maximise carbon capture is key when reforesting an area,

15
00:01:22,526 --> 00:01:28,620
but ideally any reforestation project should have several goals.

16
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:35,982
These could include selecting trees that can contribute to wildlife conservation, improve the availability

17
00:01:35,982 --> 00:01:41,800
of food for the local community and maintain the stability of soil systems.

18
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:50,321
Meeting as many of these goals as possible, whilst doing no harm to local communities, native ecosystems

19
00:01:50,321 --> 00:01:57,840
and vulnerable species, is the sign of a highly successful tree-planting scheme.

20
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:04,110
To ensure the survival and resilience of a planted forest, it’s vital to use

21
00:02:04,110 --> 00:02:09,199
tree seeds with appropriate levels of genetic diversity:

22
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:15,790
the amount of genetic variation found within a species essential for their survival.

23
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:23,645
Using seeds with low genetic diversity generally lowers the resilience of restored forests,

24
00:02:23,645 --> 00:02:31,260
which can make them vulnerable to disease and unable to adapt to climate change.

25
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:37,893
Choosing the right location for reforestation projects is as important as choosing the right

26
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:39,420
trees.

27
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:46,262
Ultimately, the best area for planting trees would be in formerly forested areas that

28
00:02:46,262 --> 00:02:48,870
are in poor condition.

29
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:56,050
It’s better to avoid non-forested landscapes such as natural grasslands, savannas

30
00:02:56,050 --> 00:03:03,490
or wetlands as these ecosystems already contribute greatly to capturing carbon.

31
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:08,746
It would also be advantageous to choose an area where trees could provide other

32
00:03:08,746 --> 00:03:13,120
benefits, such as recreational spaces.

33
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:20,614
Reforesting areas which are currently exploited for agriculture should be avoided as this often

34
00:03:20,614 --> 00:03:28,710
leads to other areas being deforested.

35
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:34,470
Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning.

36
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:40,093
Making the right decisions about where to plant trees depends on having the right

37
00:03:40,093 --> 00:03:41,860
information.

38
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:51,570
Having detailed and up-to-date maps identifying high-priority areas for intervention is essential.

39
00:03:51,570 --> 00:03:56,469
Drone technology is a useful tool in helping to prioritise

40
00:03:56,469 --> 00:04:01,710
and monitor areas of degraded forest for restoration.

41
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:08,563
In Brazil, it’s being used to identify and quantify how parts of the Amazon

42
00:04:08,563 --> 00:04:17,340
are being devastated by human activities such as rearing cattle and illegal logging.

43
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:21,818
A good example of where the right trees were picked to achieve a restored

44
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:27,080
forest is in NLampang Province in Northern Thailand.

45
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:33,897
A previously forested site which had been degraded through mining was reforested by a

46
00:04:33,897 --> 00:04:39,250
cement company together with Chiang Mai University.

47
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:47,711
After spreading 60 cm of topsoil, they planted 14 different native tree species which

48
00:04:47,711 --> 00:04:51,480
included several species of fig.

49
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:57,669
Figs are a keystone species because of the critical role they play in maintaining

50
00:04:57,669 --> 00:05:00,040
wildlife populations.

51
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:10,060
They are central to tropical reforestation projects as they accelerate the speed of the recovery process by attracting animals

52
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:15,030
and birds which act as natural seed dispersers.

53
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:21,200
This helps to promote diversity through the healthy regrowth of a wide range of

54
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,350
plant species.

55
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:29,875
Unlike the majority of fruit trees, figs bear fruit all year round, providing a

56
00:05:29,875 --> 00:05:33,630
reliable food source for many species.

57
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:40,446
At this site, for example, after only three rainy seasons, monkeys started visiting to

58
00:05:40,446 --> 00:05:46,820
eat the fig fruits, naturally dispersing seeds through defecation.

59
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:53,123
Reforestation projects should always aim to make sure that local communities are consulted

60
00:05:53,123 --> 00:05:57,740
and involved in the decision-making process.

61
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:03,782
The restoration of mangrove forests in Madagascar is an example of a project which

62
00:06:03,782 --> 00:06:08,840
has succeeded in creating real benefits for the community.

63
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:15,051
Destruction of the mangrove forests had a terrible impact on plant and animal life,

64
00:06:15,051 --> 00:06:18,878
and also badly affected the fishing industry,

65
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:25,530
which was a major source of employment for local people living in coastal areas.

66
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:32,793
The reforestation project involved hiring local people to plant and care for the new

67
00:06:32,793 --> 00:06:34,940
mangrove trees.

68
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:40,665
Millions of mangrove trees have now been planted which has resulted in the return

69
00:06:40,665 --> 00:06:44,100
of a healthy aquatic ecosystem.

70
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:50,223
The mangroves also act as a defence against the increased threat of flooding caused

71
00:06:50,223 --> 00:06:52,250
by climate change.

72
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:59,718
What’s more, the local economy is more stable and thousands more Madagascans are now

73
00:06:59,718 --> 00:07:02,890
able to send their children to school.

74
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:04,736
One other important point to consider .

75
00:07:04,736 --> 00:07:04,786
.

76
00:07:04,786 --> 00:07:04,840
.
